<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<cfsSimulation xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
               xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.cfs++.org/simulation ../../../../../share/xml/CFS-Simulation/CFS.xsd"
               xmlns="http://www.cfs++.org/simulation">

  <documentation>
    <title>Contact patch test on triangular (tet-derived) contact facets</title>
    <authors><author>kroppert</author></authors>
    <date>2026-08-08</date>
    <keywords><keyword>contact</keyword></keywords>
    <references>none</references>
    <isVerified>no</isVerified>
    <description>
      The 3D contact patch test on TRIA3 (tet-derived) contact facets. Two stacked cubes,
      Kuhn-split into TET4 at DIFFERENT resolutions (2x2x2 and 3x3x3) so the two interface
      triangulations do not match, touching exactly at z = 1. The 18 secondary triangles are cut
      into 64 mortar cells, so the mortar clipping really runs in a triangular reference domain
      rather than returning whole elements.

      The lower body is fixed at the bottom, both bodies are laterally confined (u_x = 0 on x =
      +-1, u_y = 0 on y = +-1), and 1e6 Pa presses on the top of the upper body, whose ONLY
      support in z is the contact interface.

      The lateral confinement makes the exact solution an oedometric state -- u_x = u_y = 0 and
      sigma_zz = -1e6 Pa everywhere -- which TET4 represents exactly. The interface must
      therefore carry exactly 1e6 Pa at EVERY integration point, not just on average, so a
      uniform contact pressure is a genuine patch test rather than a statement about a
      resultant. (ContactPatchTest3d leaves the sides free and is exact only because it has a
      single element per body; refined, its true contact pressure is non-uniform.)

      This is the first testcase to exercise ST_TRIA in ContactInterface (IsInsideElement,
      ClampToElement, GetReferencePolygon and the mortar clipping in a triangular reference
      domain); every earlier contact test used QUAD9 or LINE3 facets.
    </description>
  </documentation>

  <fileFormats>
    <input>
      <hdf5 fileName="ContactPatchTestTria3d.h5" linearizeEntities="__none__"/>
    </input>
    <output><hdf5/></output>
    <materialData file="mat.xml" format="xml"/>
  </fileFormats>

  <domain geometryType="3d">
    <regionList>
      <region name="master_elem" material="Aluminium"/>
      <region name="slave_elem" material="Aluminium"/>
    </regionList>
    <surfRegionList>
      <surfRegion name="master_iface"/>
      <surfRegion name="slave_iface"/>
      <surfRegion name="top"/>
      <surfRegion name="bottom"/>
      <surfRegion name="sidex"/>
      <surfRegion name="sidey"/>
    </surfRegionList>
  </domain>

  <fePolynomialList>
    <Lagrange><gridOrder/></Lagrange>
  </fePolynomialList>

  <integrationSchemeList>
    <scheme>
      <method>Gauss</method>
      <order>4</order>
      <mode>absolute</mode>
    </scheme>
  </integrationSchemeList>

  <sequenceStep>
    <analysis><static/></analysis>

    <pdeList>
      <mechanic subType="3d">
        <regionList>
          <region name="master_elem"/>
          <region name="slave_elem"/>
        </regionList>

        <contactList>
          <contactPair name="cube_contact"
                       primarySurface="master_iface"
                       secondarySurface="slave_iface"
                       slidingType="small"
                       normalPenalty="100"
                       initialGapHandling="fromMesh"
                       integrationOrder="2"/>
        </contactList>

        <bcsAndLoads>
          <!-- lower body supported in z; the lateral components follow from the confinement
               below and are consistent with it (u_x = u_y = 0 in the exact solution). -->
          <fix name="bottom">
            <comp dof="x"/><comp dof="y"/><comp dof="z"/>
          </fix>
          <!-- lateral confinement on BOTH bodies. This is what makes the exact solution
               uniform, and it also removes the upper body's lateral rigid-body modes. The
               upper body keeps NO z support other than the contact interface. -->
          <fix name="sidex">
            <comp dof="x"/>
          </fix>
          <fix name="sidey">
            <comp dof="y"/>
          </fix>
          <pressure name="top" value="1e6"/>
        </bcsAndLoads>

        <storeResults>
          <nodeResult type="mechDisplacement"><allRegions/></nodeResult>
        </storeResults>
      </mechanic>
    </pdeList>

    <linearSystems>
      <system>
        <solutionStrategy>
          <standard>
            <setup idbcHandling="penalty"/>
            <matrix storage="sparseNonSym" reordering="noReordering"/>
            <nonLinear method="newton" logging="no">
              <lineSearch type="none"/>
              <incStopCrit>1e-9</incStopCrit>
              <resStopCrit>1e-9</resStopCrit>
              <maxNumIters>20</maxNumIters>
            </nonLinear>
          </standard>
        </solutionStrategy>
        <solverList><directLU/></solverList>
      </system>
    </linearSystems>

  </sequenceStep>
</cfsSimulation>
